+# Online matchmaking patch (exvs2-lobbies) — EXPERIMENTAL, NOT WORKING IN-GAME YET
+
+> ⚠️ This branch has **never been tested with the real game**. Everything is based on static analysis of the
+> IB exe ([exvs2-lobbies](https://github.com/ServerOmega/exvs2-lobbies)) and on fake-cabinet tests.
+> You must already have a copy of the game. Upstream: Chiang-17/EXVS2-IB-Server (v1.2.0, commit 7f4b280).
+
+## What this changes
+| Area | Upstream | This patch |
+|---|---|---|
+| RegisterPcb | SRV_MATCH `"{host}/match"`, no STUN | when `OnlineMatching.Enabled`: SRV_MATCH = full URL (`MatchUrl` or `http://{host}/match`) + **SRV_STUN** entry (`StunHost`/`StunPort`) |
+| MMS `/match` (`/mms` alias) | Ping, IssueNodeId → `[1]`, MatchingSetting; everything else `ERR_SERVER` | IssueNodeId → unique persisted ids (≥ issue_count); **EntryMatching / CheckMatching / CancelMatching** with an in-memory 2v2 matchmaker |
+| Matchmaker | — | per-mode queues (world id + attrs), solo shuffle, fixed pairs never split, CPU stand-ins, ranked (worlds 13/14) bucketed by class with level band widening 0→1→2→any at 0/15/35/60 s, blacklists, optional 1v1/2v1 after `FillAfterSeconds` |
+| LoadClassMatch | 1 unix-time schedule row, empty pattern & search-ratio tables | hour row (0–27) **and** unix row → pattern 1; grade→level pattern rows for classes 1–4; search ratios; request table |
+| SaveVsmOnResult | badge only | also stores Class Match `after_rate`, class, grade and class win/lose (OMM_CLASS) |
+| PreLoadCard | `grade_solo/team` always 0 | returns the stored grade |
+| DB | — | migration `AddClassMatchGrade` (adds `Grade` to both class-record tables) |
+| Build | Windows only | optional Linux build: `-p:LinuxHost=true` (drops the WinForms disclaimer dialog) |
+
+## Build
+```
+# Windows (as upstream):           dotnet publish Server-Infinite -c Release -r win-x64
+# Linux host:                      dotnet build Server-Infinite -p:LinuxHost=true -o out && cd out && dotnet Server-Infinite.dll
+# Cross-check Windows build on Linux: dotnet build Server-Infinite -p:EnableWindowsTargeting=true -r win-x64
+# Matchmaker unit tests:           dotnet test Tests/Matchmaking.Tests
+```
+.NET 9 SDK required. Note `.gitignore` excludes `wwwroot/` image resources (needed only for the web UI).
+
+## Configure (`Configurations/server.json` → `CardServerConfig.OnlineMatching`)
+```json
+"OnlineMatching": {
+  "Enabled": true,
+  "MatchUrl": "",              // "" = built-in MMS at http://<host the cabinet used>/match
+                               // or e.g. "http://203.0.113.10:5000/mms" for the external Python server
+  "StunHost": "203.0.113.10",  // coturn; IP literal recommended ("" = same host as this server)
+  "StunPort": 3478,
+  "StunUser": "", "StunPass": "",
+  "PollingIntervalSeconds": 3,
+  "FillAfterSeconds": 30, "AllowPartialRooms": true,
+  "StaleAfterSeconds": 20,     // drop a waiting cabinet that stopped polling (min 3 x poll interval)
+  "ClassMatchScheduleMode": "Both",  // Both | Hours | UnixTime
+  "VerboseLog": false,         // true = also one line per CheckMatching poll (debugging only)
+  "NetworkRealms": ""          // "" = default realms, "off" = none, or "name=cidr,name=cidr"
+}
+```
+Environment overrides also work, e.g. `CardServerConfig__OnlineMatching__Enabled=true` (env vars are
+re-added after the json files, so they win; before 2026-11-13 the json value silently won).
+Cabinet side: `battleMode: 0` in the active `testmode_pcb.json` entry (online path instead of the LM).
+
+## Load-test fixes (2026-11-13, exvs2-lobbies `server-sketch/loadtest`)
+* A repeated EntryMatching (same node + apply_id) after the cabinet was matched no longer queues a second unit
+  (the cabinet used to land in two rooms).
+* A node id held by another cabinet (different `pcb_serial`) is rejected with `ERR_DUPLICATE_ENTRY` instead of
+  replacing / merging into that cabinet's entry; `node_id` 0 is rejected with `ERR_NODEID`.
+* Cabinets that stop polling are dropped after `StaleAfterSeconds` (was matching_timeout + 20 s → ghost players).
+* When a unit ends by timeout, the partner's cancel or staleness, its other cabinet gets `MATCH_CANCELED`
+  instead of `ERR_MATCH_NOENTRY`.
+* One queue slot per cabinet: a new entry from a `pcb_serial` drops that cabinet's older waiting unit.
+* The matchmaker clock is monotonic (`Stopwatch`), so a wall-clock step / VM resume no longer expires every
+  waiting cabinet at once.
+
+## Disconnect-test fixes (2026-11-13, `server-sketch/loadtest/disconnects.py`)
+* The same leader re-entering with a new `apply_id` (came back after a drop, maybe in another mode) replaces
+  its old entry; it used to be merged into it and keep the old mode. Partner entries / same-apply retries still merge.
+* Staleness is tracked per cabinet: a pair whose leader or partner stopped polling is dropped after
+  `StaleAfterSeconds` (the other cabinet's polls used to keep the ghost matchable).
+* A pair leader whose partner re-entered solo on the same node gets `MATCH_CANCELED` (was `ERR_MATCH_NOENTRY`).
+* A late CancelMatching from the leader for an older `apply_id` no longer cancels its current entry.
+* A retried poll after the matching timeout gets `MATCH_CANCELED` again (was `ERR_MATCH_NOENTRY`).
+* After a restart, a poll for a node id issued before the restart gets `MATCH_CANCELED` (was `ERR_MATCH_NOENTRY`).
+
+## Network diagnostics log (2026-11-13)
+Address/NAT lines, so a "never matches" or "matches but can't connect" report can be read from `server.log`.
+Card data (ChipId / AccessCode / BootToken) and `pcb_serial` are never logged. One line per event, not per poll.
+* `NET register-pcb src=<request ip> -> match=<url> stun=<host>:<port>`; `NET-WARN register-pcb` when a remote
+  cabinet is handed a loopback MatchUrl/StunHost.
+* `NET entry node=N src=<request ip> local=<ip:port> global=<STUN ip:port> nat=<mapping>/<filtering> class=<c> [MISMATCH]`
+  (also `NET merge` for a pair partner). `class`: `no-nat` (local = global), `nat`, `stun-missing` (no global
+  address: STUN failed). `MISMATCH` = STUN global ip differs from the request source (ignored for loopback sources).
+* `NET-WARN node=N STUN global X != request source Y ...` once per (source, global) pair; or once for `stun-missing`.
+* `MATCH-NET room=R | <one NET description per cabinet> | pairs: a<->b local same-NAT (addr / addr) ; a<->c global (...)`:
+  the address each side will dial, using the exe rule (equal global ips -> dial the peer's local ip:port).
+* `drop nodes=[..] reason=...` (replaced by re-entry / same cabinet entered again / matching timeout /
+  cancelled by node N / stopped polling (stale)).
+* `VerboseLog: true` adds `check node=N -> <code> room=R` per poll.
+Request source is the TCP peer (`RemoteIpAddress`, IPv4-mapped shown as IPv4); proxy headers are not trusted.
+
+## One server for LM and non-LM players (2026-11-13, exvs2-lobbies `analysis/lm-and-online.md`)
+Every cabinet talks to the MMS itself; the LM never does (the WAN manager exists only in the PCB root). So one
+server serves cabinets from any number of stores / LMs and home setups at once, all in one pool per mode.
+* **Same cabinet = same `pcb_serial` + same STUN global IP** (was: serial only). The POC hook gives every
+  install serial 0001, so terminal 1 of every LM and most home setups share a serial; the old rule dropped them
+  from the queue ("same cabinet entered again"). Fake-cabinet mix test: 3/14 matched before, 14/14 after.
+* **Network realms:** players whose STUN global IP is on different networks (Radmin 26/8, Hamachi 25/8,
+  100.64/10 overlay, private/loopback = `lan`, everything else = `internet`) can't reach each other, so they
+  are never put in one room. Same realm = one pool, whatever store / LM / home. `NetworkRealms: "off"` disables it.
+  The NET log lines show `realm=`.
+
+## Known gaps / risks
+* CheckMatching / CancelMatching are not authenticated: anyone who knows a node id can cancel that entry.
+* Malformed protobuf bodies on `/match` get HTTP 500 from the model binder (the real cabinet never sends them).
+* Hole-punch / P2P packet format unknown; real battles need reachable UDP (public IP/UPnP or a shared VPN).
+* Mode→world mapping, class ids (1–4) and the hour-based schedule are inferred, not observed.
+* `Grade1Solo/Team`, promotion matches, Extreme ladder (`LoadRankMatch`) untouched.
+* Hand-written migration has no Designer file (EF applies it; snapshot updated).
+* Matchmaker state is in memory; restart drops waiting players (node ids persist, their polls get MATCH_CANCELED).
+* A room is never refilled or torn down when a member drops after the match: the protocol has no message for it.
+* Ranked results are saved per card (`SaveVsmOnResult`); a side that never reports simply records nothing.
